---
title: Banana Curry Chicken
source: https://seasongenerously.com/2021/11/03/chicken-with-banana-curry-sauce/
servings: 4
prep time: 10 minutes
cook time: 20 minutes
---

Preheat oven to 450 degrees.

In a #mixing bowl{}, mash @bananas{2-3} with a fork, then add @curry powder{2%tbsp}, @ground coriander{2%tsp}, @ground mustard{1%tsp}, @butter{3%tbsp}(melted), @lime zest{} (zest of 1 lime), @lime juice{4%tsp}, @salt{1-1/4%tsp}, @black pepper{1/2%tsp}, and @water{1/4%cup}. Stir to combine into a curry sauce.

Make a few deep cuts in each @chicken breasts{4} and place them in a #roasting pan{}. Pour the curry sauce over the chicken, making sure it gets into the cuts.

Roast in the bottom third of the oven for ~{20%minutes}, until the chicken is cooked through.

Remove the pan from the oven and transfer the chicken to a plate. Set the pan over medium heat and whisk in the remaining @water{1/2%cup} until the sauce is heated through.

Top with @parsley{1%tbsp} and serve with rice.
